<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- PastCastTab — the body of the PastCast window: date / start / window, the historical SPC outlook for
     that date, and that day's storm reports. One of three mode bodies (see Controls/Windows/TemporalWindow,
     registered once per mode); the window supplies the surface, the title and the pin, so this is content
     only.
     ⚠️ The file keeps its "Tab" name from when the three were tabs of one Timeframe window. It is the same
     control, unchanged by the split; renaming all three would be churn. Bound to the coordinator MapViewModel.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │  ┌──┐ PastCast                    │ 5:00–7:00 PM     │  ← THE NAME ROW = NowCast's header: BLUE
       │  │██│ Tuesday May 24, 2011        │                  │     square (literal, meaning TBD), name over
       │  └──┘                                                │     the LOADED date │ the LOADED window (30,
       │       (nothing loaded: "No replay date" │ "No Timeframe │     console-clock face). Placeholders at 40%.
       │        Loaded", both dimmed)                         │
       │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐        │  ← THE CARD = only the TWO SOURCES: the
       │  │ Choose timeframe… ⁘⁘⁘⁘ Or ⁘⁘⁘⁘ [📡 Atlas] │        │     pickers, or a saved event (Atlas → PAST
       │  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘        │     EVENTS, live even while loaded). "Or" 20,
       │  ──────────────────────────────────────────          │     letters centred on the dots (Tight bounds)
       │  Date    [ May 24, 2011       ▾]  ┆       ┆          │
       │  Start   [ 5:00 PM            ▾]  ┆(empty)┆          │  ← the PICKERS (ViewModel.Radar) — LOCKED
       │  Window  [30m│1h│▓2h▓│3h│6h│12h]  ┆       ┆          │     + dimmed while a window is loaded; they
       │  [      Set Timeframe         ]  [ Clear ]          │     END where Set ends (ONE grid); Set = the
       │                                                      │     old Load (same rules); Clear =
       │  Loaded 28 frames · May 24, 5:00 PM +2 hours         │     forget it + pickers to NOW; status/errors
       │                                                      │     LEFT under them. 24 px gap, then sections
       │ ⠿ › [x] Storm cells    ──────────●  100%          ┃  │  ┐ the LAYER RUN: top of the list
       │                                                ┃  │  │ ┃ = PanelScroller's thumb, in a
       │                                                   │  │   16 px gutter that never collapses,
       │                                                   │  │   bled 12 px into the window margin
       │ ⠿ › [x] Storm reports  ──────────●  100%             │  │
       │ ⠿ ⌄ [-] Damage surveys ──────●────   70%             │  │ = top of the map; drag by ⠿ to
       │     ┌────────────────────────────────────┐           │  │ restack (default order shown)
       │     │ 4 tornado tracks                   │           │  │
       │     │ Mon May 6, 2024 · 7:00 PM → 9:00 PM│           │  │ tornado surveys (NWS DAT + NCEI
       │     └────────────────────────────────────┘           │  │ Storm Events) for the LOADED
       │     [x] ■ Damage polygons              12            │  │ window
       │     [x] ━ Tracks                        4            │  │
       │     [ ] ● Survey points                96            │  │
       │     [EFU][EF0][EF1][EF2][EF3][EF4][EF5]              │  │ ← DAT's own EF colours
       │ ⠿ › [x] Warnings       ──────────●  100%             │  │ as in effect at the FRAME on
       │ ⠿ › [x] Watches        ──────────●  100%             │  │ screen (IEM VTEC archive)
       │ ⠿ › [x] Mesoscale discussions ───●  100%             │  │ MDs + MPDs: areas + a reader
       │ ⠿ › [x] SPC outlook    ───────●───   55%             │  │ box = show/hide, any product
       │ ⠿   [x] Radar          ──────────●─   85%            │  ┘ header only
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         (the Open Atlas button that sat 100 px below the sections moved INTO the card, 2026-10-01)

     ⚠️ THE DOW EVENT SECTION IS GONE (2026-09-27) — it is the Anvil Atlas's DOW events tab now
     (Composites/DowEventsAtlasTab). Its Show still turns PastCast on first. Don't re-add it here.

     Laid out ENTIRELY with grids (rows/columns, no StackPanels) so rows are easy to add/rearrange: a fixed
     [label | control] outer grid, one row per field.

     EVERY SECTION IS A Primitives/PanelSection — header = grip + chevron + a select-all box + the title +
     the OPACITY slider; body = its controls, SettingsFieldLabelStyle rows in one aligned label column.
     Timeframe is NOT a section: it is what every section acts on, so it sits fixed above them. Sections start
     closed; open/closed is PERSISTED per section (PanelSection.PersistExpansion → AppSettings.SectionExpanded,
     "past/..."), as is every tick, opacity and outlook pick here (ViewModels/Map/TemporalWindowPersistence).
     ⚠️ THE LAYER RUN'S ORDER IS THE MAP'S Z-ORDER, and the user owns it: drag a layer section by its grip
     (or Alt+Up/Down) and OnSectionsReordered hands the order to MapViewModel.SetLayerOrder, which saves it
     (AppSettings.PastCastLayerOrder — separate from NowCast's) and restacks the map. The XAML order is the
     DEFAULT, matching layers.js DEFAULT_ORDER; a saved order is applied over it once, on first load.
     ⚠️ Each LayerId is a Models/Map/LayerOrder id, mirrored in layers.js GROUPS — change all three.
     ⚠️ The window opens at a FIXED full height (WindowManager's Left anchor), not sized to this body, so the
     SECTIONS scroll inside Primitives/PanelScroller (the app's hand-rolled scroller, built here first; the
     other panel windows get it next). Timeframe stays put above it. The scroller's 16 px gutter is ALWAYS
     claimed — no thumb when everything fits, but no sideways re-flow either — and it BLEEDS 12 px into the
     window's right margin; Timeframe's right padding is worked out from both so the two line up.

     ⚠️ THE HEADER CHECKBOX IS A SELECT-ALL, exactly as in NowCastTab: IsChecked is ONE-WAY and the Click
     hands the decision to the view model, whose answer overwrites the box's own toggle. Every section carries
     one. The SPC outlook's is SHOW/HIDE (PastOutlookViewModel.IsShown, ToggleShown), separate from its
     Product pick, and live whatever the product (None included).
     Clicking a box does not expand/collapse.

     ⚠️ THE HEIGHT IS NOT THIS WINDOW'S TO SET: Styles.xaml SectionHeaderHeight, app-wide.

     ⚠️ THE CARD IS A PREVIEW, NOT A RECEIPT. Its two readouts come from the pickers below (PastEventDateText
     / PastEventRangeText), so they describe what Load WILL do; only the footer describes what already
     happened. Do not re-point them at the loaded window — the split between the two is the entire reason
     the card can show a stale selection honestly.
       • Timeframe (root row 0, ViewModel.Radar) — a CalendarDatePicker on the PastEventDate facade, a TimePicker
         bound straight to PastEventTime, and a SegmentedPicker on PastEventDurationIndex. No element names
         are load-bearing here any more; there is no widget-sync code left to reach them.
     The layer sections run in the map's Z-ORDER (top of the list on top) and each layer's opacity lives in
     its own section HEADER.
       • Historical outlook (ViewModel.PastOutlook) — a card over Day / Product / Cycle, then the LEGEND
         (shared Primitives/OutlookLegend, last in the section, gone when collapsed or nothing is drawn);
         opacity in the header. Day is a ComboBox, the same control as ForeCast's.
         Selecting a product fetches the archived issuance for the entered replay date and overlays it on
         the past radar; there is no Load, so the card is a RESULT rather than a preview.
         ⚠️ Cycle is DISABLED while Product is None; the header Opacity also while the box hides it.
         Product shares its row with [Discussion.] → the Outlook Discussion WINDOW (shared with ForeCast's;
         past discussions aren't archived yet, and the window says so).
         ⚠️ Days 1-3 is a PRODUCT BOUNDARY (SPC has no categorical past day 3), not an arbitrary cap; see
         the note on that row before widening it.
     Storm reports stay a separate control — the NowCast tab shows the same block, so it is content of TWO
     hosts.

     ⚠️ This tab does NOT enter or leave replay; that is the PastCast key in the bottom bar's centre cluster
     (Load fills the armed replay with frames). A tab body configures a mode, the key runs it.

     ⚠️ THERE IS NO SAVED EVENTS SECTION HERE ANY MORE (removed 2026-09-25): past events are browsed and
     played from the Anvil Atlas's Past events tab (Composites/PastEventsAtlasTab), which fills these
     pickers through the same ViewModel.SavedEvents path. Don't re-add a second list here. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.PastCastTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <conv:BoolToVisibilityConverter x:Key="BoolToVis"/>

        <!-- The Timeframe card's ATLAS button: transparent face, 1 px ACCENT hairline, 6 px corners (a quiet
             door, not a primary action). Minimal template so it can't pick up the stock button's chrome; hover and
             press only fill the face. LOCAL: this window is its only consumer. -->
        <Style x:Key="OpenAtlasButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6"/>
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="16,8"/>
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Grid x:Name="Root"
                              Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                              BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                              BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                              CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                              Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource ControlFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource ControlFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Content.Opacity" Value="0.4"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Content"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- Two rows: the FIXED Timeframe block, then the sections. ⚠️ The VisualStateManager groups live on THIS
         root (the first element of the UserControl's content) — GoToState looks for them here. -->
    <!-- ⚠️ STRETCH, and the sections row is STAR: the scroller needs a BOUNDED height to scroll within —
         TemporalWindow's BodyHost hands this control the full window row. -->
    <Grid>
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Timeframe: always there, no header, can't be collapsed -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>    <!-- the sections, in the scroller -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ⚠️ THE CARD'S TWO ACCENT BRUSHES ARE STATES, NOT x:Bind FUNCTIONS — a correctness fix, not a
             tidy-up. They used to come from code, through Application.Current.Resources.TryGetValue, which
             resolves against Application.RequestedTheme — the OS theme, and settable only before content
             loads. The app pins its palette on the ROOT ELEMENT's RequestedTheme instead
             (MainWindow.ApplyAppTheme), so those lookups quietly returned the OTHER theme's brush: on a
             dark-mode machine, the light theme drew its dirty-state accent in the dark theme's colours.
             {ThemeResource} in a state setter resolves against THIS element and re-resolves on a live
             switch, which an x:Bind function cannot — it only re-runs when its bound inputs change, and the
             theme is not one of them.
             ⚠️ LoadStyle() is deliberately still an x:Bind function: DefaultButtonStyle / AccentButtonStyle
             are keyed STYLES, defined once rather than per theme, and the brushes inside them are their own
             ThemeResources. A Style has no theme to get wrong. -->
        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="SelectionStates">
                <VisualState x:Name="SelectionClean">
                    <VisualState.Setters>
                        <Setter Target="CardEdge.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                        <Setter Target="FooterText.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </VisualState.Setters>
                </VisualState>
                <VisualState x:Name="SelectionDirty">
                    <VisualState.Setters>
                        <Setter Target="CardEdge.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                        <Setter Target="FooterText.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource AccentTextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                    </VisualState.Setters>
                </VisualState>
            </VisualStateGroup>
        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

        <!-- ===================== TIMEFRAME: the card, then the pickers ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ NOT A SECTION ANY MORE (2026-09-27): it is what the whole window acts on, so it can't be
             collapsed or scrolled away. Padding 12 is PanelSection's own body padding, so it sits exactly where
             it did inside the section; the bottom 24 is the gap before the first section header.
             ⚠️ The RIGHT 16 = that 12 + PanelScroller.GutterWidth (16) − the scroller's 12 px bleed, so the
             card lines up with the section bodies below, which sit left of the always-claimed gutter. Change
             all three together. -->
            <Grid Grid.Row="0" Padding="12,12,16,24" MinHeight="{StaticResource TemporalHeaderMinHeight}">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the name row: square · PastCast over date │ the window -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card: Choose a custom timeframe… ⁘ or ⁘ [Atlas] -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the three pickers + [ Set Timeframe ] [Clear], one grid -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- status / errors -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- THE NAME ROW — NowCast's header, matched (the user's call, 2026-10-01; TemporalWindow hides
                     PastCast's title for it). Both readouts describe the LOADED window (RadarViewModel's HEADER
                     block), never the pickers; with nothing loaded they are placeholders, dimmed to 40%.
                     ⚠️ The square is BLUE, a literal, and means nothing yet — recency doesn't apply to a replay
                     (the user's call: blue "until we decide otherwise"). Same shape as NowCast's feed bar. -->
                <Grid Grid.Row="0">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="22"/>   <!-- the square -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>    <!-- PastCast over the date -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- hairline · the window -->
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Border Grid.Column="0" CornerRadius="5,0,0,5" Background="#FF2F81F7"/>
                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Margin="12,0,12,0" Spacing="2" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                        <TextBlock Text="PastCast" FontSize="30" FontWeight="SemiLight"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LoadedReplayDateText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13"
                                   Opacity="{x:Bind PlaceholderOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                    <!-- The CLOCK's spot: the loaded window in the console clock's face (SemiLight, TABULAR digits,
                         the AM/PM small on their bottom edge) at 30 rather than 40, so a start–end range fits. The
                         placeholder rides the same TextBlock at 16 (RangeFontSize). -->
                    <Border Grid.Column="2" BorderThickness="1,0,0,0" Padding="12,0,0,0"
                            BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LoadedReplayRangeDigits, Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontSize="{x:Bind RangeFontSize(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontWeight="SemiLight" Typography.NumeralAlignment="Tabular"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Opacity="{x:Bind PlaceholderOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.LoadedReplayRangeSuffix, Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontSize="16" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Margin="0,0,0,5"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>

                <!-- THE CARD: only the TWO SOURCES now (the user's call, 2026-10-01 — the date/range preview that
                     sat here duplicated the header and the pickers, and Load moved under the pickers). -->
                <Border x:Name="CardEdge" Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,14,0,0" CornerRadius="8" Padding="13,12"
                        Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="14">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- Atlas -->
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                        <!-- THE TWO SOURCES (the user's design, 2026-10-01): pick your own window with the pickers
                             below, OR play a saved event from the Atlas. Dot bridges (the tools tier's separator,
                             FillWidth) span the gaps either side of "or"; equal stars, so "or" sits between them.
                             The right bridge's −6 cancels most of the card's 14 column gap, matching the left side. -->
                        <Grid Grid.Column="0">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Choose timeframe…" FontSize="13"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator Grid.Column="1" FillWidth="True" Margin="8,0"/>
                            <!-- "Or": capital, 20 px — its letters (~14 px) stand a little proud of the 9.5 px dot
                                 bridges, the user's call. ⚠️ TextLineBounds="Tight" trims the layout box to the
                                 letters (cap line → baseline), so VerticalAlignment Center centres the LETTERS on the
                                 bridges' middle row, not the line box (which sat them low). It only trims LAYOUT —
                                 the O's round overshoot still draws; nothing here clips. -->
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="Or" FontSize="20" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextLineBounds="Tight"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                            <prim:MapControlsStripSeparator Grid.Column="3" FillWidth="True" Margin="8,0,-6,0"/>
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- OPEN ATLAS, on Past events (MapViewModel.OpenAtlasOnEvents — also selects the event PastCast
                             has picked). Live even while a window is loaded (Play asks before replacing it). MinWidth
                             84 = the width it shared with Load when Load sat under it. ⚠️ The mark is the bar's Atlas
                             key glyph (EC05, MainWindow AtlasKey) — the same door, the same mark; change both. -->
                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource OpenAtlasButtonStyle}" MinWidth="84"
                                Padding="10,6" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                Click="OnOpenAtlasClick"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Browse saved severe-weather days in the Anvil Atlas and play one here">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="14" Glyph="&#xEC05;"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource AccentTextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                                <TextBlock Text="Atlas" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Button>
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <Border Grid.Row="2" Height="1" Margin="0,14"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

                <!-- THE PICKERS + THE BUTTONS, ONE GRID (the user's call, 2026-10-01): the pickers end where Set
                     Timeframe ends, and CLEAR has its own column with nothing above it for the three picker rows —
                     one grid is what makes those two edges the same line.
                     ⚠️ LOCKED (disabled + dimmed) while a window is loaded: Clear is the way to change it. The dim is
                     on each label + picker (PickerOpacity), NOT the grid, so the buttons in it stay full strength. -->
                <Grid Grid.Row="3" ColumnSpacing="12" RowSpacing="10">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="60"/>   <!-- labels -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>    <!-- pickers; Set Timeframe spans labels + this -->
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/> <!-- Clear only: empty above it -->
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Date -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Start -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Window -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- [ Set Timeframe ] [Clear] -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- ⚠️ ONE calendar, not three combos. Its Date is a DateTimeOffset?, which the view model
                         exposes as a FACADE over the year/month/day indices everything downstream still reads —
                         see PastEventDate. It also cannot express Feb 30, which three independent combos could,
                         so the day-clamp in the loop engine is no longer reachable from this form.
                         ⚠️ Min/MaxDate are REQUIRED, not decoration: the year combo used to bound the choice to
                         the archive's range, and a bare calendar will happily offer next century.
                         ⚠️ EVERY date bound here comes from RadarViewModel.LocalMidnight, and it must. This
                         picker interprets and returns LOCAL time, so a date given at any other offset comes
                         back as a different calendar day — the getter and this control then walk each other a
                         day per round trip, synchronously through the binding, and STACK-OVERFLOW the app. That
                         is not hypothetical; it happened. Don't hand it a UTC-framed date. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="Date" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"
                               Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <CalendarDatePicker Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1"
                                        Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                        DateFormat="{}{month.abbreviated} {day.integer}, {year.full}"
                                        MinDate="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventMinDate}"
                                        MaxDate="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventMaxDate}"
                                        Date="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventDate, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind PickersEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="The date to replay (local time)"/>

                    <!-- ⚠️ ONE picker, bound STRAIGHT to the view model's TimeSpan. It replaced an editable hour
                         combo, an editable minute combo, an AM/PM checkbox pair, and the ~110 lines of
                         code-behind that converted between them and kept them in step. PastEventTime was always
                         a TimeSpan; the form simply was not shaped like one. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Text="Start" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"
                               Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <TimePicker Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1"
                                Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                ClockIdentifier="12HourClock"
                                MinuteIncrement="5"
                                Time="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventTime, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind PickersEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Start of the replay window (local time)"/>

                    <!-- ⚠️ Six segments, not a dropdown: the list is short and fixed, so the choice is worth one
                         click. The SHORT labels are their own list on the view model, kept beside the long ones
                         and the minutes array because all three are indexed by PastEventDurationIndex. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="Window" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"
                               Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                    <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1"
                                          Opacity="{x:Bind PickerOpacity(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                          ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventDurationShortLabels}"
                                          SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.PastEventDurationIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind PickersEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow), Mode=OneWay}"
                                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="How much of the day to replay, starting at the time above"/>

                    <!-- SET TIMEFRAME (was the card's Load) spans labels + pickers, so its right edge IS the pickers'
                         right edge; CLEAR, only as wide as it needs, alone in the third column. Margin top 4 + the
                         row gap 10 = the 14 that sat above the old button row.
                         ⚠️ Set keeps Load's rules: accent while pressing it would DO something, greyed once loaded
                         and still matching (the archive day is immutable). Clear is live only while something is
                         loaded: it forgets the window (yours or a played event), drops the loop and puts the
                         pickers on NOW (RadarViewModel.ClearReplay). -->
                    <Button Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Margin="0,4,0,0"
                            Content="Set Timeframe" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                            IsEnabled="{x:Bind LoadEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, ViewModel.Radar.IsReplaySelectionDirty), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Style="{x:Bind LoadStyle(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, ViewModel.Radar.IsReplaySelectionDirty), Mode=OneWay}"
                            Click="OnLoadClick"/>
                    <Button Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="2" Margin="0,4,0,0" Content="Clear"
                            IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, Mode=OneWay}"
                            Click="OnClearClick"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Clear the loaded timeframe or event and reset the pickers to now"/>
                </Grid>

                <!-- STATUS / ERRORS — left-aligned under the buttons (it was the card's footer). Coloured by the
                     SelectionClean / SelectionDirty states above. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="FooterText" Grid.Row="4" Margin="0,8,0,0"
                           Text="{x:Bind CardFooter(ViewModel.Radar.IsReplaySelectionDirty, ViewModel.Radar.PastEventStatus), Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.Radar.PastEventStatus), Mode=OneWay}"
                           FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
            </Grid>

    <!-- THE SECTIONS SCROLL; Timeframe above them doesn't. Primitives/PanelScroller: its gutter is always
         claimed, so opening a section never shifts the layout sideways.
         ⚠️ A StackPanel, not a Grid of rows: the sections' CHILD ORDER is the display order, which is what
         a drag re-arranges. Every section here is a layer now (Timeframe moved out above, DOW to the Atlas), so
         the whole panel is the ONE contiguous run PanelSection.ApplyLayerOrder assumes. -->
    <!-- ⚠️ Margin right -12 BLEEDS the scroller's gutter into the window's 16 px body margin (see the
         PanelScroller header): the gutter ends 4 px from the window edge. -->
    <prim:PanelScroller Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,0,-12,0">
    <!-- ⚠️ Sections must stay the pure layer run (ApplyLayerOrder / LayerOrderOf read its children as the map's
         z-order), so nothing else goes IN it. -->
    <StackPanel x:Name="Sections" VerticalAlignment="Top" Spacing="8">

        <!-- ===================== STORM CELLS ===================== -->
        <!-- The radar's storm-cell attributes for the LOADED window and site, following the scrubber. Shared
             control (Composites/StormCellsInput) with the Now window, like the storm reports below. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Storm cells" LayerId="cells" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnStormCellsHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every storm-cell mark"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the storm-cell marks and tracks">
            <comp:StormCellsInput ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== STORM REPORTS ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ The heading is HERE, not inside StormReportsInput: that control is shared by BOTH
             temporal windows, and a window owns its own section structure while the control is just
             content. Putting it inside would give this section a heading in a window whose other
             sections might not have one. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Storm reports" LayerId="reports" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsCheckBoxEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnStormReportsHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every report type"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the storm-report dots">
            <comp:StormReportsInput ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== NWS DAMAGE SURVEYS ===================== -->
        <!-- Tornado damage surveys for the LOADED window (ViewModel.DamageSurveys): NWS Damage Assessment
             Toolkit polygons/tracks/points, plus NCEI Storm Events tracks for anything the DAT lacks (all of
             pre-2012, most of it). A tornado shows when its time on the ground overlaps the window. Authored inline (PastCast is its only host), card-over-rows like the reports.
             ⚠️ Polygons AND tracks are ticked by default (the user's call): the section exists to put the path
             under the radar loop, and only some offices draw polygons.
             ⚠️ The EF chips are the DAT's own polygon colours, literals mirrored from damage-surveys.js
             EF_COLORS — change both. Data colours, never themed. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Damage surveys" LayerId="damage" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsCheckBoxEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnDamageSurveysHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every damage-survey layer"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Polygon fill and point opacity (tracks and outlines stay stronger)">
            <Grid VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- three layer rows + EF key -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <Border Grid.Row="0" CornerRadius="8" Padding="13,12"
                        Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.CardHeadline, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="15"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.CardContext, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="13" Margin="0,4,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.DamageSurveys.CardContext), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.CardFooter, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="11" Margin="0,6,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.DamageSurveys.CardFooter), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="0,14"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

                <Grid Grid.Row="2" RowSpacing="9">
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Damage polygons -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Tracks -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Survey points -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- EF key -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- One row per layer; the mark in front says what it draws (a filled square, a line, a
                         dot), in a neutral EF2 so it reads as "a rating colour", not as one rating. -->
                    <CheckBox Grid.Row="0" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.ShowAreas, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="EF-rated damage polygons (drawn by some NWS offices)">
                        <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="11" CornerRadius="2"
                                    Background="#FFFF00" BorderBrush="#6E6E6E" BorderThickness="1"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Damage polygons" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Count(ViewModel.DamageSurveys.AreaCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </CheckBox>

                    <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.ShowTracks, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Tornado paths — surveyed tracks (NWS DAT), else NCEI Storm Events (straight within each county)">
                        <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="4" CornerRadius="2"
                                    Background="#FFFF00" BorderBrush="#141414" BorderThickness="1"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Tracks" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Count(ViewModel.DamageSurveys.TrackCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </CheckBox>

                    <CheckBox Grid.Row="2" MinWidth="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.DamageSurveys.ShowPoints, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Individual survey damage points">
                        <Grid ColumnSpacing="9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="11" Height="11" CornerRadius="6"
                                    Background="#FFFF00" BorderBrush="#141414" BorderThickness="1"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="Survey points" FontSize="13" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Count(ViewModel.DamageSurveys.PointCount), Mode=OneWay}"
                                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </CheckBox>

                    <!-- The EF key: the DAT palette every layer is coloured by. -->
                    <Grid Grid.Row="3" ColumnSpacing="3" Margin="0,2,0,0">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Border Grid.Column="0" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#9C9C9C">
                            <TextBlock Text="EFU" FontSize="11" Foreground="#141414" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="1" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#00FFC5">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF0" FontSize="11" Foreground="#141414" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="2" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#55FF00">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF1" FontSize="11" Foreground="#141414" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="3" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#FFFF00">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF2" FontSize="11" Foreground="#141414" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="4" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#E69800">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF3" FontSize="11" Foreground="#141414" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="5" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#E60000">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF4" FontSize="11" Foreground="#FFFFFF" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                        <Border Grid.Column="6" Height="18" CornerRadius="3" Background="#A80084">
                            <TextBlock Text="EF5" FontSize="11" Foreground="#FFFFFF" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                </Grid>
            </Grid>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== WARNINGS + WATCHES (as in effect at the displayed frame) ===================== -->
        <!-- ViewModel.PastAlerts: IEM's VTEC archive for the LOADED window, drawn with the NowCast looks on
             layers of their own and filtered to the frame on screen — a warning reshapes at each follow-up and
             watch counties drop out as they were cancelled. The SAME control as NowCast's two sections, bound to
             PastCast's own view models (their ticks + opacity are saved separately from NowCast's). -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Warnings" LayerId="warnings" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Warnings.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnPastWarningsHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every warning type"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Warnings.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Warnings.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the warning polygons (fill and outline together)">
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput AlertNoun="warnings"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Warnings, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <prim:PanelSection Header="Watches" LayerId="watches" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Watches.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnPastWatchesHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every watch type"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Watches.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Watches.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the watch counties (fill and outline together)">
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput AlertNoun="watches"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastAlerts.Watches, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== MESOSCALE DISCUSSIONS ===================== -->
        <!-- SPC MDs + WPC MPDs for the LOADED window: drawn as in effect at the displayed frame, all of them
             listed to read. Shared control with the Now window. A click on an MD's area opens THIS section. -->
        <prim:PanelSection x:Name="DiscussionsSection" Header="Mesoscale discussions" LayerId="mds" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnDiscussionsHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide every discussion kind"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions.AnyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the discussion areas and labels">
            <comp:DiscussionsInput ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== SPC OUTLOOK: the card, then the pickers ===================== -->
        <!-- The header box is SHOW/HIDE (PastOutlook.IsShown, persisted), separate from the product pick:
             hiding keeps Day / Product / Cycle, so ticking it back redraws the same outlook from cache.
             ⚠️ The box works whatever the product, None included — it never greys. The opacity greys while
             hidden or None (nothing drawn to fade). -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="SPC outlook" LayerId="outlook" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.IsShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnOutlookHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide the outlook (keeps the day, product and cycle you picked)"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind OutlookOpacityEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, ViewModel.PastOutlook.ShownOnMap), Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Outlook fill opacity (outlines stay solid)">
            <Grid>
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rule -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the pickers -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the legend: last, so a collapsed section takes it along -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- THE CARD, deliberately the same shape as the Timeframe card above it — headline, context,
                     footer — so the window reads as one system rather than two forms stacked.
                     ⚠️ IT IS A RESULT, NOT A PREVIEW, which is the one way it differs from Timeframe's: there is
                     no Load here, the outlook applies the moment you pick it, so the card describes what is on
                     the map right now. That is also why it carries no button.
                     ⚠️ The FOOTER is the error channel as well as the times slot — see the ⚠️ on SetCard in
                     PastOutlookViewModel for why a two-tier card needs that to survive a failed fetch. -->
                <Border Grid.Row="0" CornerRadius="8" Padding="13,12"
                        Background="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush}"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.CardHeadline, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="15"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.CardContext, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="13" Margin="0,4,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.PastOutlook.CardContext), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.CardFooter, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   FontSize="11" Margin="0,6,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Visibility="{x:Bind HasText(ViewModel.PastOutlook.CardFooter), Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="0,14"
                        Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

                <Grid Grid.Row="2" ColumnSpacing="12" RowSpacing="10">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="60"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Day -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Product -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Cycle -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- ⚠️ A ComboBox, the same control as ForeCast's Day row (the user's call, 2026-09-28: one
                         shape for both windows). It was a 3-segment SegmentedPicker.
                         ⚠️ DAYS 1-3 IS A PRODUCT BOUNDARY, not an arbitrary cap — SPC has no categorical outlook
                         beyond day 3; days 4-8 are one combined probabilistic on a single daily issuance. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="Day" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <ComboBox Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, Mode=OneWay}"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.Days}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.SelectedDayOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Outlook day (1-3) for the replay date"/>

                    <!-- The product list CASCADES with the day (day 1 breaks out tornado/wind/hail; days 2-3
                         carry a single combined probabilistic), so it stays a dropdown — its length changes. -->
                    <!-- …and SHARES its row with "Discussion.", which opens the Outlook Discussion window (no row of
                         its own — the user's call, 2026-10-01; ForeCast's Product row matches). Past discussions
                         aren't archived yet; the window says so. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Text="Product" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <Grid Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" ColumnSpacing="8">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ComboBox HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, Mode=OneWay}"
                                  ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.ProductOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                                  DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                                  SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.SelectedProductOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="Historical outlook product — None clears the overlay"/>
                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Content="Discussion."
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind OutlookDetailEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, ViewModel.PastOutlook.HasOutlook), Mode=OneWay}"
                                Click="OnDiscussionClick"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Read SPC's forecast discussion for this outlook in its own window"/>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- ⚠️ Cycle and Opacity are DISABLED while the product is None. None is this section's off
                         switch, so neither has anything to act on; they used to stay fully live over an empty
                         readout, which reads as a bug rather than as a state.
                         ⚠️ Cycle now has its OWN ROW. It used to be crammed in beside Day behind a lowercase
                         inline "cycle" label, which was the single most haphazard thing in this window. -->
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="Cycle" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
                    <ComboBox Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind OutlookDetailEnabled(ViewModel.Radar.HasLoadedReplayWindow, ViewModel.PastOutlook.HasOutlook), Mode=OneWay}"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.CycleOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.SelectedCycleOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="SPC issuance cycle (UTC); Auto picks the one in effect at the replay time"/>
                </Grid>

                <!-- THE LEGEND (shared Primitives/OutlookLegend), last in the body like ForeCast's. Hides on
                     HasLegend — nothing drawn (None, hidden, no archive) means nothing to key. -->
                <prim:OutlookLegend Grid.Row="3"
                                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.HasLegend, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    Entries="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.LegendEntries, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    HatchRows="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.HatchLegendRows, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    ShowHatching="{x:Bind ViewModel.PastOutlook.ShowHatching, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
            </Grid>
        </prim:PanelSection>

        <!-- ===================== RADAR: header only — the layer's show/hide and its opacity ============ -->
        <!-- ⚠️ The opacity is GLOBAL (one radar layer, live and replay); NowCast shows the same slider, which
             is safe only because Past and Now can't both run. -->
        <prim:PanelSection Header="Radar" LayerId="radar" Reordered="OnSectionsReordered"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowRadarLayer, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnRadarHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show the radar layer"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RadarOpacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowRadarLayer, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Opacity of the radar layer — turn it down to read what is under it"/>

        <!-- (The DOW event section moved to the Anvil Atlas — Composites/DowEventsAtlasTab, 2026-09-27.) -->
        <!-- (The Open Atlas button that sat 100 px below here moved INTO the Timeframe card, 2026-10-01.) -->
    </StackPanel>
    </prim:PanelScroller>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
